					 Accountant 
				 
				 Accountant in East Bridgewater, MA is responsible for managing the town’s financial records, budgets, and reporting. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Animal Control & Inspection 
				 
				 Animal Control & Inspection in East Bridgewater, MA oversees animal safety, welfare, and enforcement of related town and state regulations. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Assessors Department 
				 
				 Assessors in East Bridgewater, MA are responsible for determining property values for taxation and maintaining accurate assessment records.Assessors in East Bridgewater, MA are responsible for determining property values for taxation and maintaining accurate assessment records. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Building Department 
				 
				 Building Department in East Bridgewater, MA oversees construction, permitting, inspections, and enforcement of building codes to ensure safety and compliance. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Council on Aging 
				 
				 Council on Aging in East Bridgewater, MA provides services, programs, and resources to support the town’s senior citizens and enhance their quality of life. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Emergency Management Agency 
				 
				 Emergency Management Agency in East Bridgewater, MA coordinates preparedness, response, and recovery efforts for natural disasters and other emergencies affecting the community. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Fire Department 
				 
				 The East Bridgewater Fire Department provides fire suppression, emergency medical services, rescue operations, and public safety education to protect the lives and property of the community. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Information Technology 
				 
				 The East Bridgewater Information Technology Department manages the town’s computer systems, networks, and digital services to ensure secure, reliable, and efficient technology support for all municipal departments. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Municipal Hearing Officer 
				 
				 The East Bridgewater Municipal Hearing Officer is responsible for conducting hearings on local bylaw and code violations, ensuring due process, and issuing fair and impartial decisions. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Parking Clerk 
				 
				 The East Bridgewater Parking Clerk manages parking violations, processes ticket payments or appeals, and assists residents with parking-related inquiries. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Police Department 
				 
				 The East Bridgewater Police Department is committed to protecting and serving the community through law enforcement, crime prevention, and public safety services. 
				
			 			 
				 
