         Voting Options in East Bridgewater Registered voters in East Bridgewater have several ways to vote in local, state, and federal elections. Review the options below to determine which voting method works best for you. ➡  View Important Deadlines for upcoming election dates. Vote-by-Mail Any registered voter may request a Vote-by-Mail ballot. This option allows you to vote from home and return your ballot by mail, in person, or by using the secure ballot drop box. ➡  Visit the Vote-by-Mail page for instructions, deadlines, and return options. Absentee Voting Absentee ballots are available for voters who qualify due to absence from town on Election Day, religious beliefs, or physical disability. ➡  Visit the Absentee Voting page to review eligibility requirements and application instructions. Vote in Person on Election Day Voters may cast their ballot in person at their assigned polling location on Election Day. ➡  Visit the Vote on Election Day page for polling hours and location information. Early Voting Early Voting may be available for certain  state and federal elections . Dates, locations, and hours will be posted when Early Voting is offered. ➡  Visit the Early Voting page (when available) for schedules and details. 
     

 
