Absentee Voting		 
	
		 
			

		 				
	 

	 	
 
	     


         Absentee Voting in East Bridgewater Absentee voting is available to voters who are unable to vote in person on Election Day due to specific qualifying reasons. Voters who do  not  qualify for absentee voting may request a  Vote-by-Mail ballot  instead. ➡  Visit the Vote-by-Mail page for information about voting by mail Who Qualifies for Absentee Voting A voter may request an absentee ballot if they are unable to vote at the polls due to: Absence from the city or town during polling hours Religious belief Physical disability Only voters who meet one of these qualifications may vote absentee. How to Request an Absentee Ballot Voters may request an absentee ballot by submitting a completed absentee ballot application using one of the following methods: By mail Town Clerk’s Office PO Box 387 East Bridgewater, MA 02333 By email townclerk@eastbridgewaterma.gov ( Signed application required — scanned or photographed applications are accepted ) In person Town Clerk’s Office 175 Central Street East Bridgewater, MA 02333 ➡  Download the Massachusetts Absentee Ballot Application Applications must be received by the deadline listed on the  Important Deadlines  page. Voting Absentee Ballot In Person Absentee ballots may be completed in person at the Town Clerk’s Office during regular business hours. ➡  View Important Deadlines for absentee voting dates Returning Your Absentee Ballot Completed absentee ballots may be returned using one of the following methods: By Mail Town Clerk’s Office PO Box 387 East Bridgewater, MA 02333 Mail ballots early to ensure timely delivery. In Person Ballots may be returned directly to the Town Clerk’s Office during regular business hours. All absentee ballots must be received by the close of polls on Election Day to be counted. Important Reminders Absentee voting is only available to voters who meet eligibility requirements Applications must be signed Ballots received after the close of polls cannot be counted Early return is strongly recommended Need Assistance? If you have questions about absentee voting, contact: Town Clerk’s Office 508-378-1606 townclerk@eastbridgewaterma.gov 
     

 
