Vote-by-Mail		 
	
		 
			

		 				
	 

	 	
 
	     


         Vote-by-Mail in East Bridgewater Any registered voter may request a Vote-by-Mail ballot for  local, state, and federal elections . Ballots are mailed to voters who request them and may be returned: By mail In person to the Town Clerk’s Office Using the secure ballot drop box ➡  View Important Deadlines for upcoming election dates Did You Receive a Vote-by-Mail Application? The Commonwealth is mailing 2026 Vote-by-Mail applications to registered voters who have not already submitted an accepted application. Voting by mail is optional. You do not need to return the application if you plan to vote in person. ➡  Learn more about 2026 voter mailings How to Request a Vote-by-Mail Ballot Voters may request a Vote-by-Mail ballot by submitting a completed Massachusetts Vote-by-Mail application using one of the following methods: By mail Town Clerk’s Office PO Box 387 East Bridgewater, MA 02333 By email townclerk@eastbridgewaterma.gov (Signed application required — scanned or photographed applications are accepted) In person Town Clerk’s Office 175 Central Street East Bridgewater, MA Online Through the  Massachusetts Vote-by-Mail system ➡  Download the Massachusetts Vote-by-Mail Application Returning Your Vote-by-Mail Ballot After completing your ballot, seal it in the ballot envelope provided and sign the envelope where indicated. Ballots cannot be counted if the required envelope is not signed. Completed ballots may be returned by mail, placed in the secure ballot drop box, or delivered in person. Ballots may not be returned directly to a polling location on Election Day. By Mail Mail your completed ballot using the return envelope provided or address it to: Town Clerk’s Office PO Box 387 East Bridgewater, MA 02333 Please mail your ballot as early as possible to allow sufficient time for delivery. A postmark alone does not guarantee that a ballot will be accepted. By Ballot Drop Box Completed ballots may be placed in the secure ballot drop box located at: East Bridgewater Town Hall 175 Central Street East Bridgewater, MA 02333 The drop box is monitored by camera, checked regularly by Town Clerk staff, and generally available 24 hours a day unless otherwise posted. In Person Completed ballots may be delivered directly to the Town Clerk’s Office during regular business hours: Town Clerk’s Office East Bridgewater Town Hall 175 Central Street East Bridgewater, MA 02333 Ballot Return Deadlines Ballot return deadlines vary depending on the type of election and how the ballot is returned. Most ballots must be received by the Town Clerk’s Office before the polls close on Election Day. However, ballots returned by mail for a biennial November State Election may qualify for a limited post-Election Day receipt period if mailed on or before Election Day. Please review the  Important Deadlines   page for the exact ballot-return deadline for each upcoming election. Important:  Do not wait until Election Day to return your ballot. Voters are strongly encouraged to return ballots as early as possible. Track Your Ballot Voters may track the status of their Vote-by-Mail ballot using the Massachusetts ballot tracking system. ➡  Track Your Ballot Online Important Reminders Sign the ballot envelope before returning your ballot Review the  Important Deadlines  page for the exact ballot-return deadline Returning ballots early is strongly recommended Do not place your ballot inside another voter’s envelope Vote-by-Mail ballots may not be returned at the polling location on Election Day New Ballot Colors Beginning with the September 1, 2026 State Primary, Massachusetts has adopted new ballot colors for early, absentee, and Election Day voting. 📄  View the Massachusetts Ballot Color Guide (PDF) Need Assistance? If you have questions about Vote-by-Mail ballots, contact: Town Clerk’s Office 508-378-1606 townclerk@eastbridgewaterma.gov 
     

 
